ources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9062298-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9062298</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1136981A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INOUE TAKEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SANYO ELECTRIC CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, TAKEO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SANYO ELECTRIC CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INOUE TAKEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, TAKEO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A voice signal pitch period sampling method for sampling the pitch period of an input voice waveform by taking a predetermined number of pitch periods on the basis of the input voice waveform of a predetermined time period. The sampled number of pitch periods is reduced by assuming that the pitch period of the next waveform of a predetermined number of pitch periods subsequent to the present waveform of a predetermined number of pitch periods sampled be the same as that of the present waveform.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé d'échantillonnage de périodes de hauteur de signal vocal permettant d'échantillonner la période de hauteur d'une forme d'onde vocale en entrée, consistant à prendre un nombre prédéterminé de périodes de hauteur sur la base de la forme d'onde vocale en entrée d'une période de temps prédéterminée. Le nombre de périodes de hauteur échantillonnées est réduit sur la base de l'hypothèse que la période de hauteur de la forme d'onde suivante, d'un nombre prédéterminé de périodes de hauteur suivant la présente forme d'onde d'un nombre prédéterminé de périodes de hauteur échantillonnées, est identique à celle de la présente forme d'onde.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>